From 8f4acc490621e0cceb86eedbe2008f3ebda2058a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Sat, 4 Jul 2026 13:39:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 25/65] fix(polecat): stop session after gt done instead of
 poll-looping the MR
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

gfork-47p.1: replace the doomed in-process goroutine in done.go with a detached `sh -c 'sleep 3; exec gt session stop --force <target>'` (gated on !pushFailed && !mrFailed; GOOS!=windows), and reconcile the four mol-polecat-* formulas to the ephemeral contract — drop 'nuke sandbox'/'check the MR again' language, add an anti-poll hard-stop, bump versions. Resolves the done.go<->formula contradiction where a persistent-but-idle polecat invented a poll loop, grew to RED, and squatted a dispatch slot.

Validated this session: gofumpt/vet/build/test-race green. E2E/devbox soak pending (lead gate).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
